### Summary of Forms & Worksheets You Will Need:
When filing (or when walking through your tax software), you will generate the following forms:
*   **Form 1040:** Your main tax return.
*   **Schedule 1:** To report your business income and claim your $2,500 Student Loan Interest deduction.
*   **Schedule 2:** To calculate your self-employment tax on your web design profits.
*   **Schedule B (Interest and Ordinary Dividends):** To report the Chase interest and Interactive Brokers dividends.
*   **Schedule C (Profit or Loss from Business):** To report your $11,200 web design income and deduct your $720 in supplies.
*   **Form 8829 (Expenses for Business Use of Your Home):** To calculate and claim your home office deduction using the actual expenses method (rent, utilities, etc.).
*   **Schedule SE (Self-Employment Tax):** To calculate the Medicare and Social Security taxes owed on your net web design profit. 

**State Taxes (Arizona):** Arizona has a flat income tax rate (2.5%). Your federal Adjusted Gross Income (AGI) will flow to your state return, so your business deductions and student loan interest deduction will also lower your Arizona state tax bill.
